WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.430
- Is it true that you were
a banana delivery girl

00:00:02.430 --> 00:00:03.263
in New Zealand?

00:00:03.263 --> 00:00:05.170
- I think I was the first, yeah.

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:07.550
The first official banana
delivery person in Wellington.

00:00:07.550 --> 00:00:09.343
I used to ride around on a scooter,

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:12.040
and I had this stack of banana boxes

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:13.420
on the back of my scooter,

00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:15.300
and then unfortunately I blew over.

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:16.133
It's a very windy city.

00:00:16.133 --> 00:00:19.000
I blew over twice outside the same cafe,

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:20.640
so I moved to a hearse,

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:22.640
and I was delivering
bananas out of a hearse

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:23.473
for a little while.

00:00:23.473 --> 00:00:26.030
- Is a hearse the same thing
in New Zealand as it is here?

00:00:26.030 --> 00:00:27.850
- Yeah, that's not a lost
in translation thing.

00:00:27.850 --> 00:00:29.690
That's, like, you put
a coffin in the back.

00:00:29.690 --> 00:00:30.610
- [Kelly] Wow.
- Yeah.

00:00:30.610 --> 00:00:32.220
- Delivering bananas?
- [Rose] Yep, exactly.

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:35.240
- Did people want the
bananas from a hearse?

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:36.820
- They didn't actually
know the details, Kelly.

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:37.770
- Okay, okay.

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:38.900
You're like, just pulling up,

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:40.150
and they're like, "Wait, what?"

00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:40.983
- It's a trick of the trade.

00:00:40.983 --> 00:00:42.080
I'm like, "Guys, don't be alarmed.

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:43.719
It's not what you think. No emergency."

00:00:43.719 --> 00:00:44.760
- [Kelly] It's bananas!

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:46.200
- Bananas! It's a great day.

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:47.033
- I love that.

00:00:47.033 --> 00:00:49.160
Another thing that you
did early in your career

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:50.670
is you wanted to be a rapper, right?

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:51.503
Were you rapping?

00:00:51.503 --> 00:00:54.173
- I did. I won't put
you through that today.

00:00:54.173 --> 00:00:55.330
I wasn't like one of those people

00:00:55.330 --> 00:00:58.280
who was sitting on a wealth of
talent that was undiscovered.

00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:00.000
It wasn't like one of those
stories you're gonna hear

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.521
where like, "I can't believe
she didn't get scouted!"

00:01:02.521 --> 00:01:04.080
- My God, you're like
a comedian! Oh my God!

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:07.720
- No, I was a terrible rapper,
a terrible rapper, but-

00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:08.600
- [Kelly] Who were your favorites?

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:10.700
- Well, growing up by the beach,

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:12.740
Bohemian kind of New Zealand lifestyle,

00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:16.550
I discovered Tupac and
finally felt really seen.

00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:18.670
- [Kelly] Oh my God!
- [Rose] Yeah.

00:01:18.670 --> 00:01:20.740
I don't know why him.

00:01:20.740 --> 00:01:22.020
- [Kelly] You related?
- Yeah.

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:24.091
- [Kelly] You related to
the core messages there?

00:01:24.091 --> 00:01:24.924
- Yep, yep.

00:01:24.924 --> 00:01:27.855
- (laughs) That's amazing!
You should be a comedian!

00:01:27.855 --> 00:01:30.000
- (laughs) You're so kind!
- [Kelly] You're so funny!

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.850
- Oh, gosh.
- Oh my God, I love you!

